# Raw Hubble flow dumps and the manifest/baseline derived from them are
# regenerated every time collect.sh / detector.py run, and a full 10x
# collection across all scenarios can easily reach tens of MB -- too large
# (and too easy to accidentally commit wholesale) to track directly.
#
# A small smoke-test sample IS committed under data/sample_run/ (see
# docs/findings.md and STATUS.md) as evidence the collect -> detect ->
# evaluate pipeline works end-to-end; that directory is intentionally
# exempted below.
data/*.json
data/manifest.csv
!data/sample_run/
!data/sample_run/*.json
!data/sample_run/manifest.csv

# results/ outputs (tables, PNGs) from evaluate.py are small for the smoke
# test and are committed as evidence; re-running experiment_a/experiment_b
# against a full 10x dataset will overwrite them, which is expected.

.hubble-portforward.log
.hubble-pf.log

__pycache__/
*.pyc
data/*.json.stderr
data_e1/
data_v3/
